docs {
  # Delete Account

  Permanently delete the signed-in user and all of their data. Better Auth's built-in `delete-user` endpoint, configured in `opulus-backend/src/auth.ts`.

  **Endpoint:** `POST /api/auth/delete-user`

  ## Authentication

  Requires an active session cookie.

  ## Request Body

  - `password` (string, required): the user's password. Better Auth would also accept a fresh session instead, but an `auth.ts` hook makes the password mandatory.

  ## Behavior

  1. Checks the password
  2. Removes each of the user's items from Plaid (`/item/remove`). A failure for an item is logged (item id, no tokens) and does not stop the deletion; the item then stays connected on Plaid's side until removed there
  3. Deletes the user. Sessions, linked logins, 2FA, items, accounts, transactions and liabilities are deleted with it (foreign keys cascade)
  4. Ends all of the user's sessions and clears the session cookie

  ## Success Response (200)

  ```json
  { "success": true, "message": "User deleted" }
  ```

  ## Error Responses

  - `401`: No active session
  - `400`: `PASSWORD_REQUIRED` (no password sent) or `INVALID_PASSWORD` (wrong password); nothing is deleted

  ## Notes

  - Destructive and cannot be undone. Use a throwaway user (see **Sign Up**), never your own data
}
